    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d510">

                <pb facs="0994" n="982" xml:id="pg982"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by General Marshall to General Chou
                        En-lai</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">OSE 126</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-06-06">June 6, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear General Chou</hi>: The Generalissimo has decided
                    that he will not enter into a joint press release. Attached is the release he
                    proposes to give the press at noon today, Thursday, June 6th.<anchor n="98"
                        xml:id="d510-f1"/></p>
                <p>In furnishing in advance this copy of the Generalissimo’s release I would
                    appreciate your giving me the opportunity to discuss with you the proposed draft
                    of your release, whatever it may be.<anchor n="99" xml:id="d510-f2"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d510-f1" n="98" xml:id="d510-f1-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Infra.</hi></p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d510-f2" n="99" xml:id="d510-f2-content">
                <p>Notation by General Marshall on June 6: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Gen Chou telephoned this a.m.</p>
                        <list>
                            <label>1.</label>
                            <item>Regrets lack of joint statement</item>
                            <label>2.</label>
                            <item>Inclusion of statement regarding the taking over of sovereignty of
                                Manchuria in Gimo statement</item>
                            <label>3.</label>
                            <item>He is drafting one—copy will be sent up later today.”</item>
                        </list></quote></p>
                <p>For latter, see press release of June 6, 4 p.m. (below).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
